  "from_addr": "Mike Allen <mike@axios.com>",
  "subject": "🔑 Axios Finish Line: Escape the doom loop",
  "date": "Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:29:24 -0500",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🎄 Plus: Holiday lights | Tuesday, November 24, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PRESENTED BY AMAZON \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Nov 24, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 481 words … 2 mins. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: The case for optimism \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Cover: Authors Equity\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n This is a sneak peek at Axios CEO Jim VandeHei's new book, \"You Control You.\" It started as a letter to his kids and grew into a hopeful, empowering way to overcome \"anxiety, infinite scroll &amp; the doom loop.\" Preorder it . \n\n This book is about you — who you are and who you will soon become.\n\n I didn't write this because I have all the answers. I don't. I wrote it because I'm done watching this great country dim while too many doomscroll. I wrote it because I believe — deeply, stubbornly, on my best days and my worst — that you give a shit and yearn to be and do better. We all do. Deep down, everyone wants to fall in love, learn, explore, accomplish, do big things, and be part of something bigger than themselves. This book is both your map and a fresh (and refreshing) way to see and follow it. 💡 It's based on one simple premise: You control you.\n\n That's it. That's the key to life. Not your genetics. Not the algorithm. Not the economy. Not your boss, your parents, your hometown, your bank account, or whatever flavor of dark and doom lights up your feed this morning. Those things matter. But you don't control them. They try to control you. They often do . You do control what you put in your brain ... what you put in your body ... what you share ... what you do when life punches you (and it will) ... what you do for work ... whom you date ... whom you spend your time with ... what others see when they look at you ... and whether you show up.\n\n You also control how you see and experience the world today and every day forward. 🕶️ Here's what you should see: You are alive at the most extraordinary moment in human history, and almost nobody is telling you that.\n\n Your feed and many friends tell you the opposite. Your friends are miserable. Your professors are tired. The cable news your parents watch is one long sustained scream. Young people report record loneliness, record anxiety, record disengagement. This shouldn't be. It needn't be.\n\n You have access to more knowledge, more tools, more freedom and more opportunity than any generation that has ever drawn breath. By a lot. It's not close. 🎯 The gap between those two facts — the despair you might see or feel and the abundance you live in — is the entire reason for this book. \n\n I swear that by the end, you won't think I'm on drugs. Preorder \"You Control You\" for you, or for a young person in your life. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AMAZON\r\n\n \r\n How Amazon and Prime help American families save money every day \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Amazon delivers billions in savings every year:\n\n\r\n \r\n Savings average $1,000 per customer for 100 million customers through everyday low prices, deals, free delivery &amp; fuel savings. \r\n U.S. customers avoided more than 4 billion trips to the store and over $11 billion in fuel costs in 2025. \r\n \r\n See more. \n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. ⛈️ After the storm \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Jay L. Clendenin/Getty Images Holiday lights decorating the Manhattan Beach Pier are reflected in puddles after a storm passed over Southern California last week. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
