59f66cd\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asxq2r.8vrn/399aeb91.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48602691.414419/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLTkwMTlkMWQyLTBkMmEtNGE3Yi1iYjYxLWYzZGI2YWExNGU0ZC5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBb4d1af55\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.3\">  <span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">PRESENTED BY AMAZON </span>  </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"16\" style=\"height:16px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios Finish Line </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Nov 24, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>Welcome back! </strong><em>Smart Brevity™ count: 481 words … 2 mins. Copy edited by Amy Stern.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: The case for optimism </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/cSXkbQBvcB7Uf5FzOJeMvjG4Ylk=/0x0:1920x1080/1920x1080/2026/11/24/1795545779197.jpeg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"White hardcover book titled \"YOU CONTROL YOU\" features a blue-to-orange gradient for the word YOU and bold black CONTROL, set on a bright blue background; the colored spine repeats the title and author Jim VandeHei.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Cover: Authors Equity</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><em>This is a sneak peek at Axios CEO Jim VandeHei's new book, \"You Control You.\" It started as a letter to his kids and grew into a hopeful, empowering way to overcome \"anxiety, infinite scroll &amp; the doom loop.\" <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48602691.414419/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL3lvdWNvbnRyb2x5b3U_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB4afb02cf\" target=\"_blank\">Preorder it</a>.</em></p><p><strong>This book is about you —</strong> who you are and who you will soon become.</p><ul><li><strong>I didn't write this</strong> because I have all the answers. I don't. I wrote it because I'm done watching this great country dim while too many doomscroll. I wrote it because I believe — deeply, stubbornly, on my best days and my worst — that you give a shit and yearn to be and do better. We all do.</li><li><strong>Deep down, everyone</strong> wants to fall in love, learn, explore, accomplish, do big things, and be part of something bigger than themselves. This book is both your map and a fresh (and refreshing) way to see and follow it.</li></ul><p><strong>💡 It's based on one simple premise: </strong>You control you.</p><ul><li><strong>That's it.</strong> That's the key to life. Not your genetics. Not the algorithm. Not the economy. Not your boss, your parents, your hometown, your bank account, or whatever flavor of dark and doom lights up your feed this morning.</li><li><strong>Those things matter. </strong>But you don't control them. They <em>try</em> to control you. They often <em>do</em>.</li></ul><p><strong>You do control</strong> what you put in your brain ... what you put in your body ... what you share ... what you do when life punches you (and it will) ... what you do for work ... whom you date ... whom you spend your time with ... what others see when they look at you ... and whether you show up.</p><ul><li><strong>You also control</strong> how you see and experience the world today and every day forward.</li></ul><p><strong>🕶️ Here's what you <em>should</em> see: </strong>You are alive at the most extraordinary moment in human history, and almost nobody is telling you that.</p><ul><li><strong>Your feed and many friends</strong> tell you the opposite. Your friends are miserable. Your professors are tired. The cable news your parents watch is one long sustained scream. Young people report record loneliness, record anxiety, record disengagement.</li></ul><p><strong>This shouldn't be. </strong>It needn't be.</p><ul><li><strong>You have access </strong>to more knowledge, more tools, more freedom and more opportunity than any generation that has ever drawn breath. By a lot. It's not close.</li></ul><p><strong>🎯 The gap between those two facts</strong> — the despair you might see or feel and the abundance you live in — is the entire reason for this book. </p><ul><li><strong>I swear </strong>that by the end, you won't think I'm on drugs.</li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48602691.414419/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL3lvdWNvbnRyb2x5b3U_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aC4afb02cf\" target=\"_blank\">Preorder</a> \"You Control You\" for you, or for a young person in your life.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48602691.414419/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtOTAxOWQxZDItMGQyYS00YTdiLWJiNjEtZjNkYjZhYTE0ZTRkLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBf4b3fa06\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48602691.414419/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48602691.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-le